3. THIRD-PARTY SIMCITY 4 MODS WHOSE DATA THIS PROJECT OVERRIDES
===============================================================================

READ THIS FIRST -- NOTHING BELOW IS REDISTRIBUTED.

    This project ships a GENERATOR, not artwork. No file authored by EA, by
    Maxis, or by any of the mod authors named below is contained in, bundled
    with, or distributed by this project. The scaled replacement packages are
    built on the end user's own machine, from the copy of SimCity 4 and the
    copies of those mods that the user already has installed. A user who does
    not own the game, or does not have a given mod installed, receives nothing
    from that mod.

    Our generated overrides are written to Plugins\zzz-SC4UIScale\ , which
    sorts after the mods' own folders in SimCity 4's load order. They are
    tier-gated and mod-gated: removing a mod removes our override for it.

    Standing project rule: every time we override another mod's data we write
    up exactly what, why, and what would make the override unnecessary. Those
    write-ups are the developer-facing callouts in tools/research/UPSTREAM-*.md
    and the summaries below are drawn from them. Nothing here is a bug report
    against these authors except where the report itself says so.

3.1  CAM -- the Colossus Addon Mod, and the SIM package
     Report: tools/research/UPSTREAM-CAM-REPORT.md
     Measured against CAM 4.0.1 + Submenus DLL 2.1.0 on SimCity 4 Deluxe
     1.1.641. Two distinct interactions:
       (a) A DATA DEFECT IS REPORTED against SIM 4.0.1: nine building
           exemplars in "2 CAM Building\CAM_Police_Fire_Buildings.dat" carry
           Item Submenu Parent (0xAA1DD399) = {0x00000000}, a menu id that
           does not exist, plus one item in CAM_Park_Buildings.dat pointing at
           an undefined submenu. Our local workaround is a generated
           Exemplar Patch dat (z_SC4UIScale_MenuFix.dat), to be deleted when
           the data is fixed upstream. A separate claim about five missing
           landmark icons was WITHDRAWN the same day as our own audit error
           and is recorded as withdrawn.
       (b) INFORMATIONAL: CAM Core legitimately replaces nine stock .UI
           scripts, six of which our dialog builder also targets. We scale
           CAM's versions, never revert them.
       (c) INFORMATIONAL (added v2.97.1, 2026-08-13): CAM also ADDS three .UI
           scripts of its own -- the city info screen {96a006b0,9b868f68}
           (the Village Hall / Town Hall query) and the civic and school query
           panels 12121201 / 12121205. Those are not overrides of anything;
           they are CAM's dialogs. We now generate scaled copies of them, and
           of nine of CAM's own bitmaps that the info screen draws, into the
           same CAM-gated package. Remove CAM and the gate removes our copies.
       (d) A second dangling resource reference, alongside the 0xFF5D2E9F
           label in 3.1(a): script 12121205 draws image {46a006b0,b5cfffff},
           which exists in neither the nine game archives nor anywhere in the
           Plugins tree. It is cosmetic -- the node is transparent-backed, so
           nothing visibly fails -- and is reported upstream for information.

3.2  warrior -- "God Terraforming in Mayor Mode" 1.0
     Report: tools/research/UPSTREAM-WARRIOR-REPORT.md
     Package warrior.god-terraforming-in-mayor-mode.1.0.sc4pac (UI_Compact.dat,
     Mayor_Sign_Menu.dat, Locales.dat). Status in the report: "FYI only. No
     defect in this mod." Both of its replacement .UI scripts are correctly
     authored. We generate 2x/1.5x/3x copies of THIS MOD'S OWN scripts and
     bitmaps -- never of the stock ones, which would revert the mod's compact
     layout -- because SC4 loads Plugins root files before subfolders, so the
     mod's 1x art legitimately outranked our root packages. Its Locales.dat is
     untouched.

3.3  CoriBoom -- "36 Slot Building Styles UI"
     Report: tools/research/UPSTREAM-BUILDINGSTYLES-REPORT.md
     File "CoriBoom's 36 Slot Building Styles UI - v0.46 Beta HA250411.dat",
     shipped inside null-45.allow-more-building-styles-dll 3.6.1-1. The report
     states plainly: "Nothing in the mod's own files was modified" and "Not a
     bug in the mod. The mod's .UI script is a perfectly good 1x layout." We
     generate a scaled copy of its 73-window panel script and matching art.

3.4  cyclone-boom -- the "save warning" mod
     Report: tools/research/UPSTREAM-SAVEWARNING-REPORT.md
     SaveWarning_Disable_Exit_Quit.dat, sc4pac package cyclone-boom.save-warning.
     Status: "informational. No bug is being reported against the mod -- it
     does nothing wrong." We generate a scaled copy of the MOD'S script (never
     the stock one, which would silently re-enable the very button the mod
     disables). Only pixel geometry and font-name-to-GUID substitution change;
     captions, colours and winflag_enable=no are preserved verbatim, and its
     own LTEXT captions are not touched.

3.5  0xC0000054 -- SC4ResourceLoadingHooks
     Not linked and not redistributed. Our generated menu-fix dat (3.1a) is
     authored in that project's Exemplar Patch cohort FORMAT so that the
     user's own installed copy of SC4ResourceLoadingHooks applies it. Only the
     data format is used; no code from it is present here.

3.6  memo33 -- Submenus DLL
     See section 2 for the source clone kept as reference material. The DLL
     itself is not redistributed.


